Vendored (not CDN-loaded) so the activity report renders in air-gapped
deployments and executes no unpinned third-party payload in the SAM UI origin.
The file is the npm-published dist/chart.umd.js — do NOT use a CDN .min.js
alias: jsdelivr re-wraps it with a banner ("Do NOT use SRI with dynamically
generated files") so those bytes are not stable.

To upgrade:
1. curl -sSL https://registry.npmjs.org/chart.js/-/chart.js-<ver>.tgz -o chart.tgz
2. Verify the tarball against the registry's published dist.integrity:
     curl -sS https://registry.npmjs.org/chart.js | \
       python3 -c "import sys,json;print(json.load(sys.stdin)['versions']['<ver>']['dist']['integrity'])"
     echo -n "sha512-"; openssl dgst -sha512 -binary chart.tgz | openssl base64 -A
   The two must match before trusting the file.
3. tar xzf chart.tgz && cp package/dist/chart.umd.js chart.umd.min.js
4. Update version/integrity/sha256 above, then rerun the pkg/tools tests.
